{"fingerprint":"63cdd1908f35fcbebb80eb1555e510691f5de180303ac59501398cb5632de3aa","path":"src/review_gauntlet/cli.py","rule_id":"data-validation","content":"The `_expand_session_template` function uses a null-byte sentinel (`\x00REVIEW_GAUNTLET_LITERAL_BRACE\x00`) to protect escaped braces during template expansion. If the input `value` (sourced from config file fields like `adapter.command`, `adapter.args`, or `adapter.env`) ever contains this sentinel string, the replacement logic will corrupt the output silently. Consider using a more robust approach such as iterating character-by-character or using a regex that distinguishes `{{`/`}}` from `{name}` in a single pass.","suggestion_code":"","existing_code":"def _expand_session_template(value: str, variables: dict[str, str]) -> str:
